{
 "id": "096-hizli-tempo-yavas-tempo",
 "lang": "en",
 "title": "When the Music Stops, Stop!",
 "theme": "Fast and slow tempo and being able to stop (statue dance)",
 "blurb": "It's statue dance time in class: when the music plays, you dance; when the music stops, you're a statue! Zeynep's feet just won't stop. Can's magic word makes saying “Stop!” easier.",
 "voiceNames": {
  "nur": "Miss Nur",
  "can": "Can",
  "zeynep": "Zeynep"
 },
 "pages": [
  {
   "text": "Music time! Miss Nur shook her tambourine: jingle jingle! “When the music plays, dance. When the music stops, be a statue!” Can and Zeynep clapped. “Hooray, the statue game!”",
   "hits": {
    "nur": {
     "say": "When the music stops, be a statue!"
    },
    "can": {
     "say": "Hooray, the statue game!"
    },
    "zeynep": {
     "say": "I love dancing!"
    }
   },
   "hint": "Touch the teacher!",
   "ask": "Have you ever played the statue dance? How did you play it?"
  },
  {
   "text": "Jingle jingle, fast, fast! Zeynep spun, jumped and hopped. Suddenly the tambourine stopped. Can froze into a statue at once. But Zeynep's feet didn't stop: pitter patter, pitter patter! Zeynep got cross. Her cheeks went hot. “My feet won't listen to me!”",
   "hits": {
    "zeynep": {
     "say": "My feet won't listen to me!"
    },
    "can": {
     "say": "I'm a statue! I'm not moving."
    },
    "nur": {
     "say": "The music stopped! Statue time!"
    }
   },
   "hint": "Touch Zeynep!",
   "ask": "Why did Zeynep get cross? What happened to her cheeks when she got cross?"
  },
  {
   "text": "Zeynep flopped down on the carpet and hung her head. Can came over. “My feet get wriggly too,” he said. “I've got a magic word: First say ‘Stop!’ Then take a deep breath. Hhhhh!”",
   "hits": {
    "zeynep": {
     "say": "Oh, this game is so hard!"
    },
    "can": {
     "say": "First say “Stop!”, then take a breath."
    }
   },
   "predict": {
    "q": "What do you think Zeynep will do when the music stops again?",
    "res": "Let's see if it works!",
    "opts": [
     {
      "l": "Says ‘Stop!’ and becomes a tree"
     },
     {
      "l": "Takes a breath and becomes a cat"
     }
    ]
   },
   "hint": "Touch Can!",
   "ask": "Have your feet ever refused to stop? What did you do then?"
  },
  {
   "text": "New round! The tambourine went jingle jingle: they jumped fast, fast! The drum went boom… boom… they glided slowly, slowly. Suddenly the music stopped. Zeynep said “Stop!” Hhhhh, she took a breath. She became a great big tree!",
   "hits": {
    "can": {
     "say": "Slowly, slowly… I'm gliding!"
    },
    "zeynep": {
     "say": "Stop! Hhhhh… I'm a tree!"
    },
    "nur": {
     "say": "Fast or slow? Listen!"
    }
   },
   "mech": {
    "done": "Fast, slow, stop! Zeynep became a tree!",
    "msg": "Fast, slow, stop!"
   },
   "hint": "Touch the tambourine first!",
   "ask": "How do you dance when the tambourine plays fast? And when the drum plays slowly?"
  },
  {
   "text": "Now very fast! Jingle jingle, jingle jingle! The tambourine stopped. Hop! Zeynep was a tree, Can was a cat. Miss Nur became a statue too. But her nose tickled: ah-choo! Everyone burst out laughing.",
   "hits": {
    "can": {
     "say": "Shhh! I'm a cat that doesn't move."
    },
    "zeynep": {
     "say": "I'm a tree, with great big branches!"
    },
    "nur": {
     "say": "Ah… ah… Ah-choo!"
    }
   },
   "mech": {
    "done": "One, two, three statues! Ah-choo!",
    "msg": "You counted three statues!"
   },
   "hint": "Count the statues!",
   "ask": "If you were a statue, what would you be? Show me!",
   "cues": [
    {
     "w": 29,
     "fx": "hapsu"
    },
    {
     "w": 33,
     "fx": "kahkaha"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "The round was over. Zeynep smiled a great big smile and puffed out her chest. “My feet listened to me!” She hugged Can. “Thank you, your magic word worked!” she said. Can laughed: “Dancing together is such fun!” Jingle jingle!",
   "hits": {
    "can": {
     "say": "Dancing together is such fun!"
    },
    "zeynep": {
     "say": "My feet listened to me!"
    },
    "nur": {
     "say": "Bravo! Fast, slow and stop!"
    }
   },
   "hint": "Touch Zeynep!",
   "ask": "How did Zeynep feel? Has a friend ever helped you?"
  }
 ],
 "guide": {
  "kazanim": [
   "skill: MHB4 Musical Movement (unverified) — Shows differences in tempo in the rhythms that accompany movement and dance through movement or dance: dances fast when the tambourine jingles fast, slowly when the drum goes boom boom slowly; stops when the music stops.",
   "HSAB.3 (unverified) — Performing rhythmic skills from gymnastics, dance and movement activities; sub-outcome: moves in different ways according to rhythm and tempo. In the statue dance, the child tries different ways of freezing, such as a tree or a cat.",
   "SDB1.2 Self-Regulation — Uses a strategy to stop moving on purpose: says “Stop!” to herself, takes a deep breath, then becomes a statue. Puts her anger into words (“My feet won't listen to me!”).",
   "E2.5 Playfulness and D4 Friendship — Can shares a moment he found hard himself and offers his friend a magic word; Zeynep says thank you, and they carry on the game together."
  ],
  "once": [
   "Point to the tambourine and the drum on the first page: “Which one goes jingle jingle, and which one goes boom boom?”",
   "Does anyone know the “statue dance” game? Remember the rules together."
  ],
  "sirasi": [
   "Stop on page 2 and ask: “What's happening in Zeynep's body? What do you feel when you get cross?”",
   "Ask the prediction question on page 3; both answers are positive, the child chooses how Zeynep will stop.",
   "On page 4, move fast, fast with the children when the tambourine plays, and glide slowly, slowly when the drum plays; become statues when the music stops."
  ],
  "sonra": [
   "What was Can's magic word? “First say Stop!, then take a breath.” Try it together.",
   "How did Zeynep's feelings change through the story? (cross → sad → calm → proud)",
   "Why did everyone laugh when Miss Nur sneezed? Why can being a statue be hard?"
  ],
  "sinif": {
   "ad": "Fast-Slow-Stop Statue Dance",
   "sure": "15 min",
   "materyal": "Tambourine, drum (or a table and a wooden spoon if you have none), a wide empty space",
   "adim": [
    "Explain that we move fast when the tambourine plays fast and slowly when the drum plays slowly, and try it a few times.",
    "When the music stops, everyone whispers “Stop!” to themselves, takes a deep breath and becomes a statue (a tree, a cat, an aeroplane…).",
    "Nobody is out in this game; a child who moves laughs and becomes a statue again. Let the children take turns playing the tambourine and choosing the tempo too.",
    "At the end, sit in a circle and ask: “When was stopping easy, and when was it hard? What helped you?”"
   ]
  },
  "evSoru": [
   "Why didn't Zeynep's feet stop?",
   "What magic word did Can tell Zeynep?",
   "If you were a statue, what would you be?"
  ],
  "evEtk": {
   "ad": "Kitchen Statue Dance",
   "d": "Put on a song at home, or keep a rhythm with a saucepan lid. Play fast sometimes and slowly sometimes; when you stop the music, everyone says “Stop!”, takes a breath and becomes a statue. Give your child a turn too: let them be in charge of the music."
  },
  "aileNotu": "Today we read “When the Music Stops, Stop!” Zeynep just can't stop in the statue dance and gets cross; her friend Can teaches her his magic word: “First say Stop!, then take a breath.” The story supports showing fast and slow tempo through movement and being able to stop on purpose (self-regulation) through play. If someone moves when you play the statue dance at home, laugh and try again; the aim is not to win but to discover stopping together."
 },
